WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
<v Margaret Okonkwo-Hale>Okay, let's start. Main item is classic end of life.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Lorraine Whitlock>I ran the model over the weekend. At twenty percent credit we lose too many of the government sites. At twenty five percent for twelve months we keep most of them and it pays back in year two.

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<v Gideon Ashdown>Sales is fine with 25. Twenty was a non-starter for the counties.

4
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
<v Priya Raghunathan>Can we park that?

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:43.000
<v Tomasz Kowalski>Engineering can't support Classic past mid next year anyway. The 4.x installs don't run on the new Windows server.

6
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.000
<v Margaret Okonkwo-Hale>So the date is June thirtieth, twenty twenty. Hard stop. No license renewals, no patches after that.

7
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
<v Priya Raghunathan>Sorry, I was on mute.

8
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Priya Raghunathan>And the credit applies to the cloud subscription fees for the first twelve months, only if they move before the date?

9
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.000
<v Priya Raghunathan>Sorry, I was on mute.

10
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.000
<v Margaret Okonkwo-Hale>Yes. Twenty five percent, twelve months, migrate before June thirty. I'll send the final note next week. Ignore the draft memo.

11
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
<v Lorraine Whitlock>classic maintenance invoices stop with the Q2 quarter then.

12
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
<v Gideon Ashdown>One more thing, Tri-County Public Works asked if they can go early. I'd like to give them the credit too.

13
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.000
<v Margaret Okonkwo-Hale>Fine. Next item: kestrel diligence. We're not ready to talk about that yet, keep it in this room.
